crtsys provides CMake helpers for Windows kernel-mode drivers:

  find_package(crtsys CONFIG REQUIRED)
  crtsys_add_driver(my_driver src/main.cpp)

The curated port currently supports x64 static-CRT builds with Microsoft
Visual Studio and a system-installed Windows Driver Kit (WDK).

The installed headers and manual-link archives are implementation details of
the CMake integration. Direct include-directory and manual-link consumption is
not a supported package contract; use the CMake functions above so the target
receives the required WDK include paths, architecture definitions, compile
options, entry point, and libraries.

Visual Studio property pages and project initializers are intentionally not
part of the curated vcpkg port. They remain available from the upstream crtsys
NuGet package.
